      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Why is the max length only 512? It feels unhelpful and weirdly stingy. I get that we don't really want people to write a novel in there, but ingame you still have to click through to see someone's bio; can't we at least have a kilobyte or two? Heck, *Discord messages* can be longer than this.\n\n(...and why isn't this documented anywhere but here?)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
